{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Carole King and Peter, Paul and Mary feel like natural next choices because melodic songwriting and folk harmonies connect with my listening to Simon & Garfunkel, Jonathan Edwards, and Melanie.",
    "Lesley Gore fits my mid-sixties pop interest, while Janis Joplin and Fleetwood Mac connect with my classic-rock listening and preference for familiar greatest-hits collections."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The Commodores collection misses my current preference for sixties pop and folk-rock; being an older greatest-hits release is not enough to make it appealing right now.",
    "See You There and Greatest Hits, Vol. 1 and 2 leave me uncertain about the artist and music, so I would pass over them for choices whose connection to my listening I recognize."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in older music seems to have been treated as a broad preference, although the songwriting, harmonies, and particular sound matter more than age alone.",
    "Greatest-hits collections suit my listening habits, but that format alone does not make every artist a strong match."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My listening to Simon & Garfunkel, Jonathan Edwards, and Melanie points toward a stronger interest in folk harmonies and melodic songwriting than some of these choices reflect.",
    "An appealing connection does not always mean I would choose something now: Olivia Newton-John interests me, but Carole King and Lesley Gore fit my current mood more closely."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations understand my interest in familiar older music, but my strongest choices depend on specific folk, songwriting, and sixties-pop connections rather than era or collection format alone."
}"}
